# CarHub — Baja SAE part tracker
# Python backend + Vite/React frontend on Windows.
#
# NOTE: git only treats # as a comment at the START of a line. Never put a
# comment after a pattern on the same line — it becomes part of the pattern
# and silently stops matching.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime data — NEVER commit these
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pitbox.db is the team's live BOM and storage/ holds every uploaded CAD file,
# datasheet and firmware binary. They are data, not source: version them with
# scripts/backup.py, not with git.
pitbox.db

# WAL sidecars. The database runs in WAL mode, so the most recent writes live
# in -wal until SQLite checkpoints. Both are churny binaries full of live data.
pitbox.db-wal
pitbox.db-shm
pitbox.db-journal

# Any database placed elsewhere via PITBOX_DATABASE_URL.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Content-addressed blobs (every uploaded file).
storage/

# Output of scripts/backup.py.
backups/

# Rotating server logs written by the scheduled task.
deploy/logs/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets and local config
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*

# .env.example IS committed — it documents every setting.
!.env.example

# Cloudflare Tunnel credentials, if anyone keeps them in-tree by mistake.
*.pem

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend (Vite / React)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# Built on the host by `npm run build` — see docs/FRONTEND.md.
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

*.local
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.eslintcache

# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored — committing it is what makes
# `npm ci` reproducible for whoever inherits this next year.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fly.io
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# flyctl's local scratch directory.
.fly/

# The storage archive made by hand when migrating data to the volume.
storage.tgz

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors and OS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local, per-machine permission grants — not useful to teammates.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local operations notes
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Running and deployment notes. Kept out of the repo on purpose — this is a
# public repository and an ops runbook does not belong in one.
OPERATIONS.md
OPERATIONS-hosting.md
